# Lead Format

Use this structure for every `leads/<Company>.md`. `<Company>.md` is a
**living document** — on every re-run for an existing company, refresh the
sections in place (don't append duplicate copies), except **Open Roles
History**, which accumulates one dated section per run so trends are visible
over time.

```markdown
# <Company>

**Careers page:** <URL>
**Researched:** <date of most recent run>

---

## Overview

<2-4 sentence summary: what they do, who for, why they're notable>

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Sector | <industry / category> |
| Headquarters | <city, state/country> |
| Employee count | <approx, with source if known> |
| Funding / stage | <e.g. "Series C, $200M, $2B valuation (July 2026)" or "Public"> |
| Founded | <year, if known> |

## Products / Services

- <bullet list of what they build or sell>

## Market Sentiment

<1-2 paragraphs: growth trajectory, investor confidence, competitive position,
any red flags (layoffs, leadership churn, negative press)>

## Recent News (last 6 months)

- <date> — <headline/summary> — [source](URL)
- <date> — <headline/summary> — [source](URL)

## Fit Notes

<Why this company matches the target risk/growth profile in
4 - Reference/candidate-profile.md — momentum signals, culture signals>

## Open Roles History

### <date of this run>

- <Job Title> — [listing](URL) — <location, posted date if known>
- <Job Title> — [listing](URL) — <location, posted date if known>

_If no matching roles were found this run, say so explicitly and note the
careers page was checked directly._

### <date of previous run>

- ...

## Trends

<Only once 2+ runs exist. Note recurring titles/teams across Open Roles
History entries (a role that keeps reappearing may signal high turnover or
sustained growth — call out which), and any notable shift in hiring volume,
location policy, or seniority level between runs.>
```

Read `4 - Reference/candidate-profile.md` for search parameters (salary floor,
location requirement, target roles, risk/stage preference) when evaluating fit
and searching for open roles.

## Refreshing an existing lead file

Before writing, check whether `leads/<Company>.md` already exists. If it
does, this is a refresh, not a fresh write:

1. Update `**Researched:**` at the top to the current date.
2. Re-verify Overview and Products/Services against current sources; edit in
   place if anything changed (renames, pivots, new product lines, acquisition).
3. Re-assess Market Sentiment and Fit Notes from scratch using current
   information — don't just carry the old text forward.
4. Refresh Recent News to the current trailing 6 months (drop items that have
   aged out, add new ones).
5. Prepend a new dated section to Open Roles History with this run's findings.
   **Never delete or overwrite prior dated sections** — the history is the
   point.
6. If 2 or more Open Roles History entries now exist, add or update the
   Trends section.
